{"depth":"full","paper_type":"observational_alma_primary","paper_type_evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We present an Atacama Large Millimeter/submillimeter Array (ALMA) 106 GHz (Band 3) continuum survey of the complete population of dense cores in the Chamaeleon I molecular cloud."}],"fields":["star_formation"],"question":{"value":"Do starless cores in Chamaeleon I show substructure/fragmentation or hide protostars undetected by Spitzer+Herschel, and is the protostar census complete?","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We show that the *Spitzer*+*Herschel* census of protostars in Chamaeleon I is complete"}]},"targets":[{"name":"Chamaeleon I dense cores (73 LABOCA-selected pointings, CHAI-xx)","details":[{"loc":"1.3 An ALMA Survey of Chamaeleon I","quote":"the Chamaeleon I molecular cloud, which is located at a distance of 150 pc (cite: belloche2011:chami)"}],"coordinates":"phase centers listed per source in Table 1 (e.g. CHAI-01 11:08:03.22 -77:39:17.9)","redshift_or_distance":"150 pc","distance_source":"Belloche et al. 2011 (cite: belloche2011:chami)"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2012.1.00031.S","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgments","quote":"This paper makes use of the following ALMA data: ADS/JAO.ALMA# 2012.1.00031.S."}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"bands","value":"Band 3 (106 GHz; 2.8 mm), Cycle 1","evidence":[{"loc":"1.3 An ALMA Survey of Chamaeleon I","quote":"we present the results of a Band 3 (106 GHz; 2.8 mm) ALMA Cycle 1 survey"}]},{"field":"frequencies_and_spectral_setup","value":"three 2 GHz continuum windows at 101, 103, 114 GHz; fourth window on 12CO(1-0) at 115 GHz (not presented)","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"Three out of the four available spectral windows were configured to measure the continuum at 101, 103, and 114 GHz, each with a bandwidth of 2 GHz"}]},{"field":"continuum_bandwidth","value":"6 GHz total","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"for a total continuum bandwidth of 6 GHz (2.8 mm) at a central frequency of 106 GHz"}]},{"field":"configurations","value":"relatively compact configuration, 25-27 antennas","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"Between 25 and 27 antennas were available for our observations, with the array configured in a relatively compact configuration"}]},{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"~2'' FWHM (300 AU)","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"to provide a resolution of approximately 2$''$ FWHM (300 AU at the distance to Chamaeleon I)"}]},{"field":"max_recoverable_scale","value":"~25''","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"The maximum angular scale that can be recovered in these ALMA data is $\sim$25$''$."}]},{"field":"sensitivity","value":"~0.1 mJy/beam 1σ rms (0.08-0.14)","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"These continuum observations achieved a 1$\sigma$ rms noise of approximately 0.1 mJy beam$^{-1}$."}]},{"field":"time_on_source","value":"~1 minute per target","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"Each target was observed in a single pointing with approximately 1 minute of on-source integration time."}]},{"field":"observing_dates","value":"2013 Nov 29 to 2014 Mar 08","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"between 2013 November 29 and 2014 March 08"}]}],"lines_targeted":[],"other_facilities":[{"name":"APEX LABOCA 870 um","provided":{"value":"target core catalog (Belloche et al. 2011)","evidence":[{"loc":"1.3 An ALMA Survey of Chamaeleon I","quote":"We target all 73 sources detected by (cite: belloche2011:chami) in a single-dish 870 $\mu$m continuum survey"}]}},{"name":"Herschel Gould Belt survey","provided":{"value":"70 um images and YSO catalog for associations/SEDs","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"Figure [2](#fig_herschel) shows images of each detected source overlaid with contours of the *Herschel* 70 $\mu$m emission from the Gould Belt survey"}]}},{"name":"Spitzer / 2MASS","provided":{"value":"protostar catalog and photometry for SEDs","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"constructed from 2MASS$+$*Spitzer*, *Herschel*, and LABOCA photometry"}]}}],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"LABOCA core catalog, positions, masses, peak densities","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"the phase center of our ALMA observations (taken directly from the core positions given by Belloche et al.)"}]},"citation":"Belloche et al. 2011 (cite: belloche2011:chami)"},{"what":{"value":"Herschel YSO catalog and classes","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2.2","quote":"list the YSO from (cite: winston2012:chami) associated with each detected source"}]},"citation":"(cite: winston2012:chami)"},{"what":{"value":"Spitzer protostar compilation","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2.3","quote":"list the associated protostar from the (cite: dunham2013:luminosities) compilation of protostars detected by *Spitzer*"}]},"citation":"(cite: dunham2013:luminosities)"},{"what":{"value":"Peak intensities of Perseus candidate FHSCs","evidence":[{"loc":"Table 5","quote":"Peak Flux Densities of Candidate First Hydrostatic Cores in Perseus"}]},"citation":"chen2010:fhsc; schnee2010:starless; dunham2011:fhsc; pineda2011:fhsc"},{"what":{"value":"OH5 dust opacity kappa=0.23 cm2/g at 106 GHz","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"We adopt the dust opacities of (cite: ossenkopf1994:oh5) appropriate for thin ice mantles"}]},"citation":"(cite: ossenkopf1994:oh5)"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[{"value":"Two orion AMR MHD simulations of collapsing starless cores (C04: 0.4 Msun; C4: 4 Msun) and Bonnor-Ebert sphere models via RADMC-3D, turned into synthetic ALMA observations","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.1","quote":"We perform two magneto-hydrodynamic (MHD) simulations of isolated, collapsing starless cores."}]}],"calibration":[{"field":"pipeline_or_manual","value":"CASA, standard routines of Petry et al. 2014 and Schnee et al. 2014","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"following the standard routines described in (cite: petry2014:alma) and (cite: schnee2014:alma)"}]},{"field":"self_calibration","value":"two rounds (phase-only, then amplitude+phase) on sources brighter than ~3 mJy","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"two rounds of self-calibration, the first phase-only and the second with amplitude and phase corrections"}]}],"imaging":[{"field":"cell_size","value":"0.25''","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"With a pixel size of 0.25$''$"}]},{"field":"array_combination","value":"overlapping fields mosaicked","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"Overlapping fields were mosaiced together."}]},{"field":"primary_beam_correction","value":"flux measurements on primary-beam-corrected images","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"All measurements were made on images corrected for primary beam attenuation."}]},{"field":"final_beam","value":"~2.5-2.7'' x 1.8-1.9'' (Table 1)","evidence":[{"loc":"Table 1","quote":"CHAI-01 | 11:08:03.22 | $-$77:39:17.9 | $2.72 \times 1.89$"}]}],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"Calibration and imaging follow standard CASA routines","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"following the standard routines described in (cite: petry2014:alma) and (cite: schnee2014:alma)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: petry2014:alma); (cite: schnee2014:alma)"},{"what":{"value":"Detection association radius 10.6'' (LABOCA half-power radius)","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2.1","quote":"within a projected separation of 10.6$''$ (cite: belloche2011:chami)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: belloche2011:chami)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["robust/weighting, deconvolver, clean threshold and masks for the real data","flux calibrator and flux scale uncertainty, CASA version","primary beam correction and mosaic details","how the 5-sigma limit and rms per field were measured","orion simulation snapshots and initial setup files (not released)","how orientation averaging gave 'at least two' detections"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Detect and measure continuum sources","method":{"value":"imfit elliptical Gaussian fits to primary-beam-corrected images; 5 sigma detection threshold","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"results from an elliptical Gaussian fit to each source using the imfit task in CASA"}]},"software":["CASA"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"5 sigma minimum significance","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"we thus adopt 5$\sigma$ as the minimum significance required for detection in this paper."}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Gaussian statistics: >500 pixels above 3 sigma but <1 above 5 sigma from noise","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"Gaussian statistics predict over 500 pixels above 3$\sigma$ simply due to random noise, but $<$1 above 5$\sigma$."}]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Derive masses and densities","method":{"value":"M = 100 d^2 S/(B(T_D) kappa); n = 3M/(4 pi mu m_H r_eff^3)","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
\label{eq_dustmass}
M = 100 \frac{d^2 S_{\nu}}{B_{\nu}(T_D) \kappa_{\nu}} \quad ,
\end{equation}$$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"T_D = 10 K, d = 150 pc, kappa=0.23 cm2/g, mu=2.37","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"With the integrated flux densities listed in Table [2](#tab_continuum) and an assumed $T_D = 10$ K"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"gas-to-dust ratio 100, OH5 dust, optically thin isothermal dust","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"the factor of 100 is the assumed gas-to-dust ratio"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"discussed that T and opacity dominate uncertainty (factor 2 in T gives factor 2 in mass)","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"a factor of two uncertainty in dust temperature directly translates into a factor of two uncertainty in mass"}]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Classify evolutionary status via multiwavelength associations and SEDs","method":{"value":"cross-match ALMA detections with LABOCA, Herschel, Spitzer catalogs; SEDs to assign protostellar/starless/disk","evidence":[{"loc":"3.3","quote":"we classify these objects as disks rather than starless or protostellar dense cores"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Test census completeness","method":{"value":"scale peak intensities of four Perseus faint protostars to 150 pc and 106 GHz with I ∝ nu^(2+beta), 0<=beta<=2, compare to rms","evidence":[{"loc":"4","quote":"assuming $I_{\nu} \propto \nu^{2+\beta}$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"same dust temperatures in Chamaeleon I as in Perseus; emission compact/unresolved","evidence":[{"loc":"4","quote":"The sources are assumed to have the same dust temperatures in Chamaeleon I as in Perseus"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Synthetic ALMA observations of simulated cores and BE spheres","method":{"value":"convert column density to 106 GHz maps with BE-derived T(N) and OH5 opacity; simobserve/simanalyze with alma.cycle1.3.cfg, 72 s, 6 GHz; clean to 0.3 mJy","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.2","quote":"We then generate synthetic ALMA observations of these simulated 106 GHz continuum intensity maps using the CASA tasks simobserve and simanalyze."}]},"software":["CASA","orion","RADMC-3D"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"cloud background A_V=35.6 added; pixel 20 AU; distance 150 pc","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.2","quote":"adopting a value of $\Sigma$ representing the maximum visual extinction toward the Chamaeleon I cloud of $A_{V} = 35.6$"}]}],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"BE temperature profiles agree with Evans et al. 2001; background offset test gave identical results","evidence":[{"loc":"Appendix A","quote":"calculated by RADMC-3D and agree with those calculated by (cite: evans2001:starless)"}]}},{"order":6,"goal":"Predict expected detections and Poisson probability","method":{"value":"Detections > N_total (n_Detectable/n_Limit)^-0.5 with tau ∝ n^-0.5, then Poisson probability of zero","evidence":[{"loc":"5.2","quote":"Equation [\[eq_detect2\]](#eq_detect2) results in a total of at least three expected detections."}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"N_total=56, n_Detectable=8.9e7 cm-3, n_Limit>2.8e5 cm-3","evidence":[{"loc":"5.2","quote":"With N$_{\rm total} = 56$, n$_{\rm Detectable} = 8.9 \times 10^7$ cm$^{-3}$, and n$_{\rm Limit} > 2.8 \times 10^5$ cm$^{-3}$"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"continuous star formation; free-fall evolution; simulations applicable","evidence":[{"loc":"5.3","quote":"(1) starless cores evolve on timescales proportional to the free-fall time, (2) star formation is continuous in Chamaeleon I, and (3) the simulations are applicable"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"power-law fits of lifetime vs central density","evidence":[{"loc":"5.3.1","quote":"with a power-law fit giving $\tau~\propto~n^{-0.50 \pm 0.01}$"}]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"calibration, imaging, imfit, simobserve/simanalyze","evidence":[{"loc":"2 Observations","quote":"The calibration and imaging were done using the Common Astronomy Software Applications (CASA) package"}]}},{"name":"orion","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"AMR MHD simulations of collapsing cores","evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.1","quote":"We use the orion Adaptive Mesh Refinement (AMR) code"}]}},{"name":"RADMC-3D","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"BE sphere temperature profiles and 106 GHz model images","evidence":[{"loc":"Appendix A","quote":"We then solved for the temperature profiles in each BE sphere using the three-dimensional Monte Carlo radiative transfer package RADMC-3D"}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"continuum sources detected at >=5 sigma","value":"24 sources in 19 fields","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"sources","from_step":1,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"We detect a total of 24 106 GHz continuum sources to 5$\sigma$ or greater significance in 19 different target fields"}]},{"quantity":"starless cores, all undetected","value":"56","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"cores","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.3","quote":"leaving us with 56 starless cores, none of which are detected by our ALMA continuum observations"}]},{"quantity":"misclassification rate of protostellar cores as starless","value":"<1/56 (<2%)","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"4","quote":"the rate at which protostellar cores in Chamaeleon I have been misclassified as starless cores is $<$1/56, or $<$ 2%"}]},{"quantity":"detected masses range","value":"0.012 to 1.7","uncertainty":"statistical only","units":"Msun","from_step":2,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"gives total masses ranging from 0.012 M$_\odot$ to 1.7 M$_\odot$"}]},{"quantity":"C04 detection threshold central density","value":"8.9e7","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"cm-3","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.2","quote":"The C04 simulation is detected over the last 8200 yr of the starless stage, when the central number density exceeds $8.9 \times 10^{7}$ cm$^{-3}$."}]},{"quantity":"C4 detection threshold central density","value":"3.3e7","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"cm-3","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.1.2","quote":"The C4 simulation is detected over the last 11000 yr of the starless stage, when the central number density exceeds $3.3 \times 10^{7}$ cm$^{-3}$."}]},{"quantity":"expected detections (orientation averaged)","value":"at least 2","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"cores","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.2","quote":"the total number of expected detections is reduced from at least three to at least two"}]},{"quantity":"Poisson probability of zero detections","value":"13.5","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"percent","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.3","quote":"the probability of detecting zero cores when two detections are expected is 13.5%"}]},{"quantity":"C04 lifetime-density index","value":"-0.50","uncertainty":"0.01","units":"dimensionless","from_step":6,"evidence":[{"loc":"5.3.1","quote":"with a power-law fit giving $\tau~\propto~n^{-0.50 \pm 0.01}$"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"All known Class 0 and I protostars detected; other detections are Flat/Class II objects","evidence":[{"loc":"6 Summary","quote":"All previously known Class 0 and Class I protostars in Chamaeleon I are detected in our continuum observations."}]},{"value":"Bonnor-Ebert spheres remain undetected to central densities of at least 1e10 cm-3","evidence":[{"loc":"Appendix A","quote":"there are no 5$\sigma$ detections, not even for the $n_c = 10^{10}$ cm$^{-3}$ model"}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Are Spitzer+Herschel protostar censuses of Cha I complete?","experiment":"Scale Perseus faint protostars to Cha I and compare with ALMA rms","result":"predicted peaks 0.7-17.7 mJy/beam vs rms 0.08-0.14","finding":"census complete; misclassification <2%","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"4","quote":"even in the most pessimistic scenario these objects would be detected to at least a 5$\sigma$ level"}]},{"hypothesis":"Do starless cores show turbulent-fragmentation substructure?","experiment":"Synthetic ALMA observations of MHD simulations vs 56 non-detections","result":"at least 2 detections expected, 0 observed (13.5% chance)","finding":"likely declining star formation / non-collapsing cores, or less-substructured models like BE spheres; cannot distinguish","support":"partially","evidence":[{"loc":"6 Summary","quote":"it is more likely that at least one of the above assumptions are wrong."}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_method","value":"ALMA sensitivity can detect substructure in starless cores that CARMA could not","evidence":[{"loc":"1.1","quote":"These same synthetic observations have shown that the Atacama Large Millimeter/submillimeter Array (ALMA) is capable of detecting substructure and fragmentation in starless cores"}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"Protostars viewed face-on rejected as explanation for Class II SEDs (no double-peaked SEDs)","evidence":[{"loc":"3.3","quote":"such objects tend to feature double-peaked SEDs (cite: whitney2003:geometry1) not seen in Figure [3](#fig_seds)"}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Mass uncertainties dominated by dust temperature and opacity assumptions","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"The true uncertainties are likely dominated by the dust temperature and opacity assumptions."}]},{"value":"Only two simulations; full parameter space needed","evidence":[{"loc":"5.3.3","quote":"a full parameter space exploration is required"}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Non-detections rely on an assumed temperature model (4-5 K centers); a 7 K floor changes thresholds by a factor of ~3","Few simulations, one magnetic setup","Imaging parameters of real data not given"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"ALMA project data cited; archive code given","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgments","quote":"This paper makes use of the following ALMA data: ADS/JAO.ALMA# 2012.1.00031.S."}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["clean parameters","simulation snapshots","CASA version","flux calibration details"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~50-100 GB raw visibilities for 73 short pointings","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Data public and photometric results are simple, but imaging settings and simulation inputs are unstated.","rediscovery_candidate":true,"rediscovery_reason":"Public data and numeric detections/flux densities with a simple mass formula; synthetic part is harder.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: petry2014:alma)","why":"standard CASA calibration/imaging routines"},{"citation":"(cite: schnee2014:alma)","why":"standard CASA calibration/imaging routines"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: belloche2011:chami)","why":"LABOCA parent catalog"},{"citation":"(cite: offner2010:turbfrag)","why":"turbulent fragmentation simulations revisited"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["APEX LABOCA survey of Chamaeleon I","Herschel Gould Belt survey","Spitzer c2d and Gould Belt surveys"]}
